<title>RUSSIA: Russian Alfa-Eko signs 40,000 bpd Iraqi oil deal.</title>
<headline>Russian Alfa-Eko signs 40,000 bpd Iraqi oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Alfa-Eko trading company said on Thursday that it had signed contracts with Iraq's State Organisation for Marketing of Oil (SOMO) for a total of 40,000 barrels per day of crude oil over six months.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said Alfa-Eko would market the oil in the United States and was in talks with U.S. oil companies, but said the deal depended on approval from the United Nations.</p>
<p>The two contracts are for 25,000 bpd and 15,000 bpd, both to be lifted from Iraq's southern terminal Mina al-Bakr.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
